invariant: INV-14
file: handshake_parser_ee.c
catches: handshake_strict_webpki
reason: the parser reads an ALPN extension even when the ClientHello
  offered no protocol, so a response to a request that never went out
  is judged on its contents instead of refused. RFC 9846 §4.3 answers
  an unrequested extension with unsupported_extension, and the alert
  here becomes illegal_parameter, which names the wrong fault.
  bin/handshake_strict_webpki's no-offer row objects.

--- old
    if (ext == EXT_ALPN && out->offered_count > 0) {
--- new
    if (ext == EXT_ALPN) {
